WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
- That's why I like the
Richard Scarry books

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.040
because you can like,
do you know those books?

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:05.873
- I don't know.

00:00:05.873 --> 00:00:07.350
- Oh, they're like,
maybe I'm dating myself.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.670
They're like before your time.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.056
- No, they're not.
We're like the same age.

00:00:10.056 --> 00:00:10.889
- I'm gonna get those for you now.

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:11.870
No, we're not the same age.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:12.703
- Yes we are.

00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:14.420
- I'm gonna get those
books for you, and...

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:16.455
- What?

00:00:16.455 --> 00:00:17.970
- I know, I'm 51 in like a couple days.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.415
- What?

00:00:19.415 --> 00:00:20.248
- Yeah.

00:00:20.248 --> 00:00:23.915
(audience whoops and claps)

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:26.262
- Yeah.

00:00:26.262 --> 00:00:27.240
- I just turned 40.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.790
I thought you were literally my exact age.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.763
What fountain are you drinking from?

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.130
- It's not
- Oh my go.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.540
- It's a lot of makeup
and people helping me.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.190
- Congratulations.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.023
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:39.023 --> 00:00:39.990
- I mean, on the book and all the things

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.283
but like more on that.

00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:43.110
Like that's great.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:44.580
Congratulations.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.870
Wait, did you say your
birthday's coming up?

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:46.980
- Yeah. May 30th.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.813
- Oh, that's exciting.

00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:49.020
- Yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.180
- Oh, you get trumped by
Memorial Day every year.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.231
That's that weekend.

00:00:52.231 --> 00:00:53.911
- By Memorial Day? I used to always, yeah.

00:00:53.911 --> 00:00:55.470
And because it's a holiday weekend

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.570
I always was gigging and working on...

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:58.403
- And even when you were young

00:00:58.403 --> 00:00:59.760
people were probably
out with their families

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.658
for birthday parties.

00:01:00.658 --> 00:01:01.680
- Yeah, nobody wanted, it's
the big summer weekend.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.090
- I kind of took it
negative, your birthday,

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.334
I don't know why I did that.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:05.253
- That's okay! It is negative, it's 51!

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:08.480
- Your birthday is so awesome!

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.190
No, I just, I literally this whole time,

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.023
thought we were exactly the same age.

00:01:12.023 --> 00:01:13.455
- Well, I'm flattered.

00:01:13.455 --> 00:01:14.288
(audience applauding)

00:01:14.288 --> 00:01:17.310
- So, you once said that the
scariest part of performing is

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.440
like the three seconds, like
right before the curtain.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.390
- Did I say that? Probably, yeah.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.309
- So you do, it's amazing
'cause you're so talented.

00:01:23.309 --> 00:01:24.660
- Do still have that stuff?

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.340
- Here's the thing,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.190
I think when I was, I've
never been like stage fright,

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.320
or I've never had like
that kind of nerves,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.480
but like I grew up seeing classical stuff

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.635
so you have to be perfect
and all those... like any...

00:01:35.635 --> 00:01:38.220
- That's how I feel and with
a theater community as well...

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.053
- You have to be perfect.

00:01:39.053 --> 00:01:41.100
And so, but it started
taking the joy away for me.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.360
And this one night, it was actually funny,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.070
it was in Australia like this random show

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.440
and I was miserable and I was like,

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.050
'cause I had focused on these minor things

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.150
that I just didn't nail
like vocally and it,

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:54.900
and then I noticed the joy of
singing was like leaving me.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.733
- Leaving off.

00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:58.469
- Yeah. And so then, it's interesting,

00:01:58.469 --> 00:01:59.910
I was like, you know what, like, whatever,

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.320
like I'm gonna sound like soulful

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.730
and pitchy sometimes, it's gonna be fine.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.920
And I feel like my voice got better.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.390
I feel like I became better

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.589
because you got outta your head.

00:02:07.589 --> 00:02:08.422
- You're relaxed.

00:02:08.422 --> 00:02:09.840
- Yeah. But do you get that?

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:10.980
- Oh my God, I get so in my head

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.870
and I feel like the older I'm getting

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:17.400
I'm getting a little bit
more, um... neurotic.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.233
- Really?

00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:19.066
- I don't know if that's with success

00:02:19.066 --> 00:02:22.830
and social media and feeling
like the lens is on me.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.360
But, um...

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.860
- But they're on you for a reason.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.640
Yeah, I mean, they're not
on you because you suck.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.580
- I'm not gonna lie,
like I just, I do, I...

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.140
- A lot of my friends in the
industry, they get nervous.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.350
- But I will say that
becoming a mom helped me

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.570
because I felt the need to be perfect

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.583
was not as crazy.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.770
- It's not the most important thing now.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.870
- It's not. I mean, if my son has a fever,

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.460
I'm not gonna not be with him

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.990
in the middle of the night
before I have to get up.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.347
So then I get on stage and I'd be like,

00:02:50.347 --> 00:02:52.027
"You screw it up tonight, well, whatever,

00:02:52.027 --> 00:02:53.100
"you had to make a choice."

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.331
So if you don't hit that big
note, you know, big deal.

00:02:55.331 --> 00:02:56.164
- That's me too.

00:02:56.164 --> 00:02:56.997
- Yeah, that's life.

00:02:56.997 --> 00:02:57.830
- But then you just alter the melody.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:58.663
- And then I was better,

00:02:58.663 --> 00:02:59.496
Yeah, and you alter the melody.

00:02:59.496 --> 00:03:00.329
- Yeah, you have to alter the melody.

00:03:00.329 --> 00:03:01.162
You have to handle it.

00:03:01.162 --> 00:03:04.470
My band will tell you
right now, I am the queen

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.110
of walking in and going,
oh, it's so interesting,

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.364
are we gonna lower this?

00:03:08.364 --> 00:03:09.900
(Idina laughs)

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.970
Are we gonna, oh, we'll just keep going.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.380
Or like, sometimes I have to take it up.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.370
It's just wherever your voice is.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.203
- Exactly.

00:03:15.203 --> 00:03:17.343
- I change, I alter melodies, I change.

00:03:17.343 --> 00:03:18.176
- Me too.

00:03:18.176 --> 00:03:19.752
- You have to if you're a live singer.

00:03:19.752 --> 00:03:21.180
- I have a thing called
the ABC performance.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.450
So especially when I'm doing
like eight shows a week

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.370
if you're really tired and stuff

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.690
I've decided there's the "A Show,"

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.520
which is the stuff that
the composer really

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.680
wants you to hit when
the critics are there.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.690
And then you come up with
a couple alternate melodies

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.880
that no one would even
know that you change.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.470
Except in your head psychologically

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:38.730
you feel like you're failing yourself

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.740
'cause you're getting sick
and you think, oh I can't.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.960
But if you just give yourself
this particular thing

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.480
and then you nail that
"B Show" or "C Show"

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.460
in a beautiful way with all of your heart.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.990
People feel just as much

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.270
and you don't one feel
completely devastated

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:54.030
that you didn't hit some high
notes of people, you know?

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.640
- 'Cause you're human and
it's a muscle, bye the bye.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:57.473
So yeah.

00:03:57.473 --> 00:03:58.306
- Yes, it is.

00:03:58.306 --> 00:03:59.940
- But you're fabulous, so you
should always remember that.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.050
So those three seconds

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.060
just think of me saying you're awesome.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:03.893
- I will.

00:04:03.893 --> 00:04:05.460
That's what I was gonna say.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.170
I was thinking 30 seconds before,

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.750
well, I just imagine I'm Kelly Clarkson.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.306
- No, imagine you're you
and I'm just sitting there,

00:04:11.306 --> 00:04:12.630
so no matter if you suck,

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.246
you're still gonna be
awesome, just so you know

00:04:14.246 --> 00:04:15.079
- I'm going to think that! Thank you!

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:17.320
- Yeah, you should think
that, I'm just saying.

